      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I've summarized the key findings from the internal audit of Q3 lending processes. Here's a concise and professional summary:\n\nOur internal audit of Q3 lending processes identified several key risks. Inconsistencies in interest rate application to mid-tier loans and missing secondary signatures in collateral documentation for West Coast branch loans pose moderate risks. Additionally, software latency in the approval pipeline resulted in a 2-hour average delay, which may impact timely loan processing. Notably, we found no significant fraud instances, but noted a decline in compliance training completion rates among new hires, from 95% to 85%. These findings highlight areas that require immediate attention to ensure the integrity and efficiency of our lending processes.",
      "source": "target",
